    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="52.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Abt">Abt</ref> 52.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="52.1" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="6" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif widobane gebroced weorðeþ, VI scill' gebete.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="10" ed="#attenborough"/>Gif widobane gebroced weorðeþ, VI scill' gebete.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#oliver" n="50" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="70" ed="#oliver"/>Gif widobane gebroce[n]<ptr type="editorNote" n="f" target="#Abt_52-1.olinote.fn.f"/> weorðeþ, VI sciƚƚ gebete.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Abt_52-1.lnote.de.1" rend="supplied"/><pb n="6" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn das Schlüsselbein<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Abt_52-1.lnote.de.2"/> verletzt wird<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Abt_52-1.lnote.de.3"/>, büsse er 6 Schill.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If the collarbone is injured, let him pay 6 shillings.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="11" ed="#attenborough"/>If a collar bone is injured, 6 shillings shall be paid as compensation.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#oliver" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="71" ed="#oliver"/>If a collarbone becomes damaged, let him pay [with] 6 shillings</ab>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Abt_52-1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">11</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">[Setze ¹ vor ‘Wenn’.] Es sollte neues Kapitel beginnen</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">[Put ¹ before ‘If’.] A new chapter should begin here</seg><note type="remark" resp="#claude">Not printed in vol. I; Liebermann: "Setze ¹ vor ‘Wenn’" (III p. 11).</note></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Abt_52-1.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">11</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Neben Friesisch und Nordisch auch mndd. <hi rend="italic">wedeben</hi>. Nicht ‘Schulterblatt’. Das <hi rend="italic">d</hi> statt <hi rend="italic">ð</hi> kann archaische Schreibung sein; <hi rend="italic">vgl.</hi> Hl 8². Das -<hi rend="italic">e</hi> ist unorganisch; <hi rend="italic">s. o.</hi> 46²</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Besides Frisian and Norse, also MLG <hi rend="italic">wedeben</hi>. Not ‘shoulder-blade’. The <hi rend="italic">d</hi> for <hi rend="italic">ð</hi> may be an archaic spelling; <hi rend="italic">cf.</hi> Hl 8². The -<hi rend="italic">e</hi> is inorganic; <hi rend="italic">see above</hi> 46²</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Abt_52-1.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">11</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Nicht ‘gebrochen’ <hi rend="italic">s. Wb brocian</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Not ‘broken’; <hi rend="italic">see Wb brocian</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Abt_52-1.olinote.fn.f" n="f" source="#oliver"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">70</biblScope></bibl><label>gebroce[n]</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Manuscript reads <hi rend="italic">gebroced</hi>.</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
